{
  "comment": [
    "Indeksy zlozone Firestore.",
    "",
    "Firestore tworzy indeksy pojedynczych pol sam, ale zapytanie laczace",
    "`where` po jednym polu z `orderBy` po INNYM wymaga indeksu zlozonego -",
    "i bez niego zwraca blad, nie pusta liste.",
    "",
    "Tak wlasnie padalo /asks: getOpenAsks() robi",
    "  where('status','==','open') + orderBy('createdAt','desc')",
    "wiec kazde wejscie konczylo sie komunikatem",
    "  'Open asks could not be loaded. This is a failed read, not an empty list.'",
    "Komunikat byl poprawny - brakowalo indeksu, ktory go usuwa.",
    "",
    "Wdrozenie: firebase deploy --only firestore:indexes",
    "(firebase.json wskazuje na ten plik)"
  ],
  "indexes": [
    {
      "collectionGroup": "asks",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        { "fieldPath": "status", "order": "ASCENDING" },
        { "fieldPath": "createdAt", "order": "DESCENDING" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "asks",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        { "fieldPath": "author", "order": "ASCENDING" },
        { "fieldPath": "createdAt", "order": "DESCENDING" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "askAnswers",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        { "fieldPath": "askId", "order": "ASCENDING" },
        { "fieldPath": "createdAt", "order": "ASCENDING" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "askAnswers",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        { "fieldPath": "author", "order": "ASCENDING" },
        { "fieldPath": "accepted", "order": "ASCENDING" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "fieldOverrides": []
}
